    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9244aa91-e4a0-52c9-940b-47ff9812a745",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e86,2,-1\u27e9$, $b=\u27e8-2,k^{2},7\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8-3,7,1\u27e9$ are coplanar.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "72009178-027c-5893-ad0b-738ed3c15fba",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "e174913f-3ccc-53df-a99a-0f65ab3ae486",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$k=\\sqrt{106}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ab87e603-ea45-5232-b7bc-072efcf87eb0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$k=-\\sqrt{106}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c26966d8-ce0a-5564-88ba-32f8c37bad2e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$k=-\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{106}$ or $k=\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{106}$"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "410286af-067b-57c9-a406-1c0ef6e855ad",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$k=-\\sqrt{106}$ or $k=\\sqrt{106}$"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6de307df-e15a-5798-bba8-ce0b46a1f9fe",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$k=-106$ or $k=106$"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "410286af-067b-57c9-a406-1c0ef6e855ad"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & k^{2} & 7 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((6)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k^{2} & 7 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}|)+((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|)+((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & k^{2} \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((6)\\cdot ((k^{2})\\cdot (1)-(7)\\cdot (7)))+((-2)\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (1)-(7)\\cdot (-3)))+((-1)\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (7)-(k^{2})\\cdot (-3)))\\\\ &=((6)\\cdot (k^{2}-49))+((-2)\\cdot (19))+((-1)\\cdot (3k^{2}-14))\\\\ &=(6k^{2}-294)+(-38)+(14-3k^{2})\\\\ &=3k^{2}-318\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k^{2}-318&=0\\\\ 3k^{2}&=318\\\\ k^{2}&=106\\\\ k&=\\pm \\sqrt{106}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\sqrt{106}$ or $k=\\sqrt{106}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
