      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & k & -4\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|)+((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & k\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (-4)-(3)\\cdot (k)))+((5)\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (-4)-(3)\\cdot (8)))+((8)\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (k)-(4)\\cdot (8)))\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot (-3k-16))+((5)\\cdot (-16))+((8)\\cdot (-2k-32))\\\\ &=(-24k-128)+(-80)+(-16k-256)\\\\ &=-40k-464\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-40k-464&=0\\\\ -40k&=464\\\\ k&=-\\frac{58}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{58}{5}.$",
